    "recommendations": "Providing address numbers that are clearly visible from the access road could support faster responder navigation to the property, particularly given the length of the driveway from the street. Keeping the driveway clear of parked vehicles and ensuring adequate width along its full length would support apparatus movement toward both the main building and the detached structure. Because the property has a single entry and exit point, identifying an area near the main building where emergency vehicles could turn around or stage may enhance operational effectiveness. The perimeter fencing configuration is worth reviewing to confirm that gates, if present, can be readily opened to avoid delays during a response."
