    "recommendations": "Reducing the concentration of shrubs and ground vegetation within the immediate structure perimeter would improve defensible space and may reduce fuel continuity around the building. Where vegetation is adjacent to the structure, creating separation between plants and the building exterior could reduce direct fuel contact and support suppression operations if needed. Managing the mixed and ground-level vegetation to introduce gaps and reduce continuous fuel coverage across the surrounding terrain may further limit opportunities for fire spread toward the structure. Maintaining open terrain areas already present on the property could support firefighter access and movement during suppression operations. Prioritizing vegetation management closest to the structure and working outward would support a practical, phased approach to improving overall wildfire resilience and property preparedness over time."
